    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000002I0r2AE": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing (Med/Surg - 3 positions)",
      "description": "Westmont College seeks qualified and motivated nursing faculty members to serve in its graduate (MEPN/CNL and MSN/CNL) and undergraduate (ABSN) nursing programs. These positions focuse on teaching, mentoring, and contributing to the growth of our nursing program. We are looking for a candidate with a strong clinical and academic background who is passionate about educating and inspiring the next generation of nursing professionals. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in nursing education, student formation, scholarly research, and professional practice. Responsibilities: Develop and teach graduate nursing courses Integrate Christian faith with teaching and learning Mentor and advise students in academic, clinical, and professional development Contribute to curriculum development and program implementation Engage in scholarly and professional activity Support clinical partnerships and student learning experiences Participate in faculty governance, program evaluation, and accreditation processes Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing (DNP or PhD) required Current RN license (California eligibility required) Expertise in clinical practice, leadership, or systems-based care Teaching or mentoring experience preferred Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College, in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Westmont is a Christian liberal arts college. We seek faculty from diverse racial and ethnic backgrounds who are committed to graduate and undergraduate teaching, scholarly activity, and the integration of faith. The college seeks to enrich its educational experience and its culture through the diversity of its faculty, administration, staff, and students. Diverse candidates from historically underrepresented groups are especially encouraged to apply Anticipated Hiring Range $121497 - $136685 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW00000079hh2AA": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor or Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree in chemistry is required. A doctoral degree is strongly preferred. The candidate should have good teaching and communication abilities. The candidate should be willing and able to create course syllabi, instructional materials, assignments and assessments. Position Summary: The visiting assistant professor position is a full-time position that includes teaching General Chemistry lecture and/or labs, Physical Chemistry 1 & 2 (Quantum Mechanics and Thermodynamics), experimental physical chemistry lab and a general education chemistry course for non-majors (Chemistry, Culture & the Environment). Responsibilities: (teaching duties may vary depending on departmental needs and candidate qualifications) -\tTeaching and preparing two General Chemistry course sections in Fall 2026 -OR- -\tTeaching four General Chemistry Lab sections in Fall 2026 -\tTeaching and preparing one Physical Chemistry 1 (Quantum Mechanics) course in Fall 2026 -\tTeaching and preparing one Physical Chemistry 2 (Thermodynamics) course in Spring 2027 -\tTeaching and preparing one Experimental Physical Chemistry Lab course in Spring 2027 -\tTeaching and preparing one Chemistry, Culture & the Environment (General Education) course in Spring 2027 Reports to: Chemistry Department Chair, Provos Anticipated Hiring Range $70841 - $75219 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    }
